 08Bring Your friends: Get Fair Ready Game Day turns career preparation in
 to a fast-paced\, interactive competition where students team up\, comple
 te challenges\, earn points\, and compete for prizes—all while building t
 he skills needed to stand out to employers.Forget sitting through another
  lecture. This is career prep turned into a game. Students will work in t
 eams through a series of challenges designed to test their career fair kn
 owledge\, communication skills\, employer research\, networking abilities
 \, and elevator pitches. Each round gives teams the opportunity to earn p
 oints\, sharpen their skills\, and move one step closer to becoming Game 
 Day champions.Challenges include:Company Intel Challenge – Put your resea
 rch skills to the test and learn how to quickly find the information you 
 need to confidently approach an employer.Employer Engagement Simulation –
  Practice approaching recruiters\, starting conversations\, asking strong
  questions\, and making a memorable first impression.Elevator Pitch Showd
 own – Step up and deliver your best introduction while learning how to cl
 early communicate your experience\, interests\, and goals.Career Fair Tri
 via – Test your knowledge of career fair do’s and don’ts\, networking str
 ategies\, employer expectations\, and more.And yes there are prizes on th
 e line! Compete to see who can rack up the most points while becoming mor
 e confident and career-fair ready.This event is designed to prepare stude
 nts for the All-Majors Career & Internship Fair on October 8\, giving you
  a chance to practice before it counts. Whether this is your first career
  fair or you simply want to strengthen your networking skills\, you’ll le
 ave with practical experience you can immediately put to use.Play the gam
 e. Win prizes. Level up your career fair skills. Then put them to the tes
 t on October 8!\n\nHosted by: POUNCE Rewards Program\, University Career 
 Services\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://pin.gsu.edu/e
 vent/12698357
